without jitter  worst 100ms window: t=1.0s takes 60 requests at once
                  first client retries at 1.00s, 3.00s, 7.00s, 15.00s, 31.00s
with jitter     worst 100ms window: t=0.2s takes 11 requests at once
                  first client retries at 0.45s, 1.57s, 5.27s, 8.99s, 17.12s

Without jitter every client waits exactly the same 1s, 2s, 4s ... so all sixty
come back at the same five instants, and the server that has just recovered is
knocked over again. Jitter spreads the identical amount of load across the
identical window, and the spike disappears.
